[1;31mNAME[0m[m
     [1;31mscript[0m – make typescript of terminal session[m
[m
[1;31mSYNOPSIS[0m[m
     [1;31mscript[0m [[1;31m-aeFkqr[0m] [[1;31m-t[0m [1;32mtime[0m] [[1;32mfile[0m [[1;32mcommand[0m [1;32m...[0m]][m
     [1;31mscript[0m [1;31m-p[0m [[1;31m-deq[0m] [[1;31m-T[0m [1;32mfmt[0m] [[1;32mfile[0m][m
[m
[1;31mDESCRIPTION[0m[m
     The [1;31mscript[0m utility makes a typescript of everything printed on your terminal.  It is useful for students who need a hardcopy record of an interactive session as proof of an[m
     assignment, as the typescript file can be printed out later with lpr(1).[m
[m
     If the argument [1;32mfile[0m is given, [1;31mscript[0m saves all dialogue in [1;32mfile[0m.  If no file name is given, the typescript is saved in the file [1;32mtypescript[0m.[m
[m
     If the argument [1;32mcommand[0m is given, [1;31mscript[0m will run the specified command with an optional argument vector instead of an interactive shell.[m
[m
     The following options are available:[m
[m
     [1;31m-a[0m       Append the output to [1;32mfile[0m or [1;32mtypescript[0m, retaining the prior contents.[m
[m
     [1;31m-d[0m       When playing back a session with the [1;31m-p[0m flag, do not sleep between records when playing back a timestamped session.[m
[m
     [1;31m-e[0m       Accepted for compatibility with [1;32mutil-linux[0m [1;31mscript[0m.  The child command exit status is always the exit status of [1;31mscript[0m.[m
[m
     [1;31m-F[0m       Immediately flush output after each write.  This will allow a user to create a named pipe using mkfifo(1) and another user may watch the live session using a utility like[m
              cat(1).[m
[m
     [1;31m-k[0m       Log keys sent to the program as well as output.[m
[m
     [1;31m-p[0m       Play back a session recorded with the [1;31m-r[0m flag in real time.[m
